## 3. The exact reach, stated honestly

The dyadic long window carries `≍ t·log t` zero mass while the short window carries at
most `≍ A_ζ·D·log t`, so the comparison is decisive precisely when `D ≲ t/A_ζ`.  The
surviving corner is `D ≍ t`, i.e. the inverse-width regime `Λ ≍ |t|⁻¹`, `D = π/(3Λ)`,
where the crude unit-window constant `A_ζ ≥ 1` is far larger than the true local density
`1/2π`.  §39 therefore **prunes** the large-cutoff/short-threshold corner; it does not
prove the clustering statement, and no claim to the contrary is made.  The open target is
unchanged in substance and sharper in form:

    (4/π²)·highGapMass  <  lowGapMass      at  D = π/(3Λ),

which needs a *sharp two-sided* local count at the dynamically chosen scale, not a crude
population bound.

## 3b. §40 — the sharp translated window count

The dyadic input above is not the end of what the checked package supports.  The contour
machinery behind `rvM_main` works for an **arbitrary** window; only its μ-integral input is
dyadic.  `Zeta23Bridge/Zeta23Bridge/NearCoreZetaWindowCount.lean` (FRONTIER §40) assembles
it directly and proves

    | N(a,b] − ∫_a^b μ |  ≤  C_w·log b        for all  T_w ≤ a ≤ b,

with `μ` the Γ-phase density (`μ(τ) ≈ log(τ/2π)/(2π)`), from
`N_eq_halfContour_completedZeta`, `halfContour_completedZeta_split`, `gamma_side`,
`backlund_horizontal`, `vertical_two`, `exists_goodHeight` and `zeta_local_zero_count` —
all checked Lean theorems.  Monotonicity of `μ` turns this into sharp two-sided counts for
every window (`zeta_window_count_le`, `zeta_window_count_ge`), i.e. genuine local density
information for the actual ζ zeros at every scale above `O(log t)`.

Applied to the gap split, both counting sides become the **same** number `μ(t+D)` and, with
no density hypothesis at all, `zeta_gap_split_sharp_cutoff_lt` gives

    J  <  1 + D + (π²/4)(2D+1) + (π²/4 + 1)·C_w·log(t+J−1)/μ(t+D) .

§36 needed two unknown density constants for this and §37 had to assume they were matched;
here they are literally equal.  The surviving cutoff window is `O(D)`, not `O(|t|)`.  The
clustering statement itself is still open: §40 gives the sharp *average* density, whereas
`(4/π²)·highGapMass < lowGapMass` is about the *actual* multiplicity mass.

